From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: a JSON tool call max_tokens cuts is the reply's cut
 call, as XML and GLM calls are (upstream port)

Ported onto f350cd3 + patches 0001-0113 from upstream ashhart/TensorFold:
  b10fda39f server: a JSON tool call max_tokens cuts is the reply's cut call, as XML and GLM calls are (Anders Jensen-Waud)
  1b5ac18bb server: a cut JSON call reads the keys a closed one does, and whole arguments spell as the closed call's (Anders Jensen-Waud)
  7faa962a0 server: a whole /v1/messages reply closes a max_tokens-cut call's input as far as written, as the stream does (Anders Jensen-Waud)

tool_stream.cutCalls falls back to tool_json_cut once GLM's cut finds none: an open <tool_call> whose JSON payload has
named an offered tool returns that call with its arguments as far as written; a call cut before its name, or naming a
tool not offered, stays text, so patch 0107/0112's TF_TOOL_CALL_GUARD sees the same offered-only calls. A whole
/v1/messages reply closes a cut call's input where it parses (tool_args_close.zig) instead of answering 500.

Port notes: only root.zig's test list and tool_stream.zig's imports conflicted (upstream-only neighbours not taken);
CHANGELOG lines not taken. Local fixes over upstream, from review: a member with a key and no value (`{"name":,`)
ended the member scan with an empty value that cutCall then indexed ([0] on an empty slice); it now stops the scan,
so the call stays text. A cut call's name matches an offered tool trimmed and in any case, as tool_parse matches a
closed call's, and returns the offered spelling. Host tests for both.
Known, unchanged from upstream and from the XML/GLM cut path this extends: a reply that streamed an earlier call and
then ends in a cut JSON call does not replay the cut call (tool_calls_streamed), and cutProse drops every envelope
before the cut call, a malformed one that 0112 would keep as text included.

Co-authored-by: Anders Jensen-Waud <5827908+ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
